.TH PROWSE.TOML 5 "2026-09-17" "ProwseTk 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
Prowse.toml \- ProwseTk project and driver configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBprowsetk run\fR command reads Prowse.toml from the working directory
unless \fB--config\fR selects another file. The file uses TOML syntax.
Drivers are declared as \fB[[drivers]]\fR tables.
.SH ENGINE FIELDS
.TP
.B user_agent
Browser identity string used for created sessions. \fBprowsetk run\fR can
override this value for a single invocation with \fB--user-agent VALUE\fR.
.SH SESSION FIELDS
.TP
.B cookies_json
Path to a browser-exported JSON cookie file. The path is resolved against the
project root and imported into the session cookie jar before plugins and drivers
run. \fBprowsetk run\fR can override this value with
\fB--cookies-json FILE\fR.
.SH DRIVER FIELDS
.TP
.B name
Name passed to \fBprowsetk run\fR.
.TP
.B script
Path to the Lua script, resolved against the project root.
.TP
.B entrypoint
Lua function to call; shipped drivers use \fBmain(args)\fR.
.TP
.B enabled
Whether the driver may be run.
.TP
.B arguments
Array of inline tables specifying \fBname\fR, \fBtype\fR,
\fBrequired\fR, optional \fBdefault\fR, and optional \fBsecret\fR.
Supported argument types include string, integer, boolean, path, and url.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[[drivers]]
name = "crawl-site"
script = "drivers/crawl_site.lua"
entrypoint = "main"
enabled = true
arguments = [
  { name = "url", type = "url", required = true },
  { name = "depth", type = "integer", default = 2 }
]
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Declare sensitive arguments with \fBsecret = true\fR. Such arguments are
never intended for driver output or logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prowsetk (1)
